      <data key="d5">Brachytherapy is a targeted treatment employed in the management of cervical cancer, offering localized therapy."|&gt;"targeted therapy, local treatment&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is a treatment option for patients with local recurrent cervical cancer requiring targeted radiation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is a treatment option used in conjunction with surgery for cervical cancer to target residual cancerous cells post-operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is effective for cervical cancer treatment, focusing radiation directly on the tumor for high precision.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is specifically used for treating cervical cancer by delivering localized radiation treatment."|&gt;"targeted therapy, local treatment&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is used as a localized treatment option for patients with cervical cancer to directly target cancerous growths.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy is utilized as a treatment after surgery for cervical cancer, often in combination with other modalities like EBRT.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy may be used as a localized treatment option for patients with cervical cancer to target tumor growths.&lt;SEP&gt;Brachytherapy offers targeted treatment for local recurrent cervical cancer, capitalizing on localized radiation delivery.</data>
