      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The various treatment options mentioned are specifically targeted for patients diagnosed with primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment planning, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Comprehensive Metabolic Panel (CMP)">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The CMP offers vital information regarding the metabolic status and organ function of patients with primary CNS lymphoma, influencing overall treatment plans."{"metabolic assessment, treatment planning"}</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Lactate Dehydrogenase (LDH)">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">LDH levels that are elevated can indicate cell damage in patients with primary CNS lymphoma, providing insights into disease progression."{"disease monitoring, enzyme levels"}</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="HIV Blood Test">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The HIV blood test is a necessary evaluation for patients diagnosed with primary CNS lymphoma to tailor appropriate treatment strategies accordingly."{"diagnostic necessity, treatment customization"}</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Hepatitis B Testing">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hepatitis B testing is critical for immunotherapy patients with primary CNS lymphoma to prevent complications during treatment."{"risk assessment, treatment safety"}</data>
      <data key="d6">9</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Stem Cell Rescue">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Stem cell rescue is a relevant treatment option for patients diagnosed with primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Stem cell rescue is critical for the recovery of patients with primary CNS lymphoma post aggressive chemotherapy treatments."{"treatment recovery, cellular support"}</data>
      <data key="d6">8&lt;SEP&gt;treatment method, cancer type</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0f15711706bc171fed17a7fab91b4b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Steroids">
      <data key="d4">6.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Steroids are used briefly in treating primary CNS lymphoma to reduce symptoms but must be administered carefully after diagnosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment management, symptom reduction</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-725b48dc82aad42ba3dc14f4b5207551</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Whole-Brain Radiation Therapy (WBRT)">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">WBRT is a common radiation technique used to treat patients with primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">radiation treatment, cancer therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Rituximab">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Rituximab is an immunotherapy approach used for patients with primary CNS lymphoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Rituximab is used in the treatment regimen for primary CNS lymphoma, enhancing the effectiveness of chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">immunotherapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="Multidisciplinary Care">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Multidisciplinary care ensures comprehensive management of patients with primary CNS lymphoma by a variety of specialists.</data>
      <data key="d6">healthcare approach, collaborative treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9e8b25c2957355218780bdfd8b72df45</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Primary CNS Lymphoma" target="NCCN Guidelines for Patients: Colorectal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The NCCN Guidelines provides comprehensive information on the treatment options for primary CNS lymphoma, facilitating patient understanding and informed decision-making.</data>
      <data key="d6">clinical guidelines, patient education</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIV" target="Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">HIV infection increases the risk of anal cancer due to its impact on the immune system.&lt;SEP&gt;HIV infection undermines the immune system, making individuals more susceptible to anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">health impact, cancer risk&lt;SEP&gt;risk factors, immune system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-06384634b72466c480713ee8d57f25ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9530f389987c13273449ab22a85170ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIV" target="Anal Squamous Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Individuals with HIV are at an increased risk of developing anal squamous cell carcinoma, necessitating particular attention in treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d6">risk factor, cancer prognosis</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HIV" target="Gynecologic Exam">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Gynecologic exams, including screenings for HPV, are particularly relevant for women with HIV, as HPV is linked to anal and cervical cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">preventive care, cancer linkage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a18089523f6dcd63cfa5664dc1c01618</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Epstein-Barr Virus" target="Nasopharyngeal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nasopharyngeal cancer is often caused by Epstein-Barr Virus, establishing a direct link between the virus and the cancer type.</data>
      <data key="d6">viral association, cancer causation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ea7b3f83164304ee4a562046eb0f5033</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Autoimmune Diseases" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Autoimmune diseases potentially weaken the immune system, increasing the risk of HPV persistence and subsequent cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">risk factors, immune response</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b4d036ee5fd77783b9e7ddef3a8477ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Premenopause" target="Amenorrhea">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Premenopause can lead to amenorrhea as hormone levels fluctuate during this transitional phase.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormonal changes, menstrual health</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Gliomas">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Gliomas are a specific type of brain tumor that present particular challenges and symptoms."\&lt;|"tumor classification, medical terminology</data>
      <data key="d6">8</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Nausea">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Nausea is a common symptom associated with brain tumors due to increased intracranial pressure.</data>
      <data key="d6">symptom, medical condition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Vomiting">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Vomiting often accompanies nausea and is a typical symptom of brain tumors exerting pressure.</data>
      <data key="d6">symptom, medical condition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Memory Loss">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Memory loss can occur in brain tumor patients as the tumor affects cognitive functions.</data>
      <data key="d6">cognitive impact, medical condition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Personality Changes">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Personality changes may result from brain tumors affecting areas that control mood and behavior.</data>
      <data key="d6">psychological impact, medical condition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Muscle Weakness">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Muscle weakness on one side of the body can be symptomatic of a brain tumor affecting motor control.</data>
      <data key="d6">motor function, medical condition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Vision Problems">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Vision problems such as blurred or double vision can signify the presence of a brain tumor.</data>
      <data key="d6">neurological symptom, medical condition</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Imaging Tests">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests are crucial for diagnosing and assessing brain tumors, including MRI and CT scans.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic tool, tumor detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Stereotactic Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A stereotactic biopsy is a method used to obtain samples for diagnosing brain tumors in specific areas.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, surgical technique</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Brain Tumor" target="Open Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Open biopsy is utilized when the brain tumor is accessible for tissue sample extraction.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, diagnostic technique</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-49c7ff3a71e74b3f0eb59258541e739e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Cerebrospinal Fluid (CSF)" target="primary CNS lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cerebrospinal fluid may contain cancer cells in cases of primary CNS lymphoma, necessitating intrathecal chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">disease symptom, treatment implication</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8fbedfa2d88a7b3852f4c2bd0bb64af0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="primary CNS lymphoma" target="CNS">
