    </edge>
    <edge source="Completion Thyroidectomy" target="NIFTP">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">NIFTP tumors, if surgically removed, do not require further treatment like completion thyroidectomy, indicating their low-risk nature.</data>
      <data key="d6">low-risk condition, treatment necessity</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Grade Carcinoma" target="Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A high-grade carcinoma is a specific classification of cancer that indicates aggressive behavior and poor prognosis.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer type, aggressiveness</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="High-Grade Carcinoma" target="Thyroid">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">High-grade carcinoma can occur in the thyroid gland, emphasizing the importance of monitoring and treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">specific cancer type, location</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroid" target="Cancer">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The thyroid gland is the organ where thyroid cancer originates, affecting its function and treatment options.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer origin, anatomy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Follow-Up Care" target="Testing and Surveillance">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Testing and surveillance are integral parts of follow-up care to detect any early signs of cancer recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring process, recurrence detection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Thyroglobulin (Tg)" target="Blood Tests">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Blood tests measure Tg levels to monitor for potential thyroid cancer recurrence after treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">monitoring, diagnostics</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9d383e4798456aa46e381fd2b02f6f96</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NCCN Guidelines for Patients®" target="bone cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The NCCN Guidelines provide essential information regarding treatment and management of bone cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer management, expert recommendations</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bone cancer" target="sarcomas">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Sarcomas are classified as a main type of bone cancer that starts within the bone or cartilage.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer classification, tumors</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bone cancer" target="osteosarcoma">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Osteosarcoma is specifically a type of bone cancer that affects rapidly growing bone cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">specific type, cancer category</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="bone cancer" target="Ewing sarcoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Ewing sarcoma is another primary type of bone cancer, highlighting the diversity of bone cancers.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype, cancer category</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="biomarker testing" target="targeted therapy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Biomarker testing helps identify potential candidates for targeted therapy or immunotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d6">testing, therapy eligibility</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Tumors" target="Primary Bone Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Primary bone cancers are a specific type of bone tumors originating from bone cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer classification, tumor types</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Tumors" target="Secondary Bone Malignancies">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Secondary bone malignancies differ from primary bone tumors as they originate from cancers in other regions of the body.</data>
      <data key="d6">tumor origin, cancer type differentiation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="NCCN Guidelines for Patients">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The NCCN Guidelines for Patients include necessary information for managing treatment and understanding bone cancer.";</data>
      <data key="d6">patient guidance, cancer education</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Osteosarcoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Osteosarcoma is a type of bone cancer mentioned within the context of the guidelines for treatment.";</data>
      <data key="d6">specific type, cancer category</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Chondrosarcoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chondrosarcoma is discussed as a type of bone cancer that requires surgical treatment.";</data>
      <data key="d6">specific type, treatment options</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Chordoma">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chordoma is identified as a type of bone cancer that may involve surgical and radiation treatment.";</data>
      <data key="d6">specific type, cancer category</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Ewing Sarcoma">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Ewing sarcoma is recognized as a category of bone cancer requiring systemic therapy.";</data>
      <data key="d6">specific type, treatment options</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Giant Cell Tumor of Bone">
