      <data key="d5">Giant Cell Tumor of Bone, while usually non-cancerous, is discussed within the context of bone cancer treatment.";</data>
      <data key="d6">specific type, treatment category</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-ba28a3ce3534c0655a0d08a953d7f038</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Core Needle Biopsy">
      <data key="d4">20.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A core needle biopsy is an essential procedure for diagnosing and staging bone cancer accurately.&lt;SEP&gt;Core needle biopsy is a diagnostic procedure performed to confirm a diagnosis of bone cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">diagnostic procedure, cancer identification&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic tool, cancer evaluation</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-6b02315423350f3598288e189fbcb8ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bone Cancer" target="Spine">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Bone cancer can appear in the vertebrae of the spine, affecting its structure and functionality.</data>
